WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:04.460
Daredevil is back – but a little different,
this time.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:08.960
As exciting as it is to see Jennifer Walters
as the green-tinted She-Hulk: Attorney at

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:14.645
Law, there's another jurist hero that fans
are likewise eager to see turn up in the new Disney+ series.

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:18.910
As teased in trailers leading up to the latest
chapter in the Marvel Cinematic Universe,

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:24.119
the MCU's newest lawyer is set to face off
against a familiar one: Matt Murdock, also

00:00:24.119 --> 00:00:28.970
known as Daredevil, played once again by Charlie
Cox from the Netflix "Daredevil" series.

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:31.770
Following his appearance in "Spider-Man: No
Way Home"…

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.020
"I'm a really good lawyer."

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:37.550
…the final trailer for "She-Hulk: Attorney
at Law" confirmed that Murdock would re-emerge

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:43.061
as the horn-headed vigilante fans fell in
love with during his stint on his Netflix series.

00:00:43.061 --> 00:00:47.559
The writers of "She-Hulk" made a daring move
introducing the hero of Hell's Kitchen, Director

00:00:47.559 --> 00:00:49.609
Kat Coiro told Entertainment Weekly,

00:00:49.609 --> 00:00:53.219
"I am definitely excited for Daredevil to
make his appearance, because I think he's

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:55.120
going to be a crowd favorite."

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:58.739
But it turns out the devil was in the details
regarding Murdock's return.

00:00:58.739 --> 00:01:00.469
One detail, specifically.

00:01:00.469 --> 00:01:04.589
Speaking to Lifehacker, "She-Hulk" writer
Jessica Gao revealed that Marvel gave the

00:01:04.589 --> 00:01:08.850
creative team a surprising level of freedom
when they put in their request for Matt Murdock

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:10.120
to appear on the series.

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:11.120
She explained,

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.560
"When they first told us that [Daredevil]
was a possibility, we just couldn't believe it.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:18.750
And as we were coming up with story and what
we wanted him to do, the fact that they kept

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:21.140
not saying no was shocking to us."

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:25.070
The one area that the writers got no say in
was Daredevil's costume.

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:26.070
Gao said,

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:29.230
"The one thing that I didn't have control
of was the suit.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:32.050
They knew exactly what they wanted the suit
to look like."

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:36.470
From what we've seen so far, Daredevil's current
appearance does largely match the costume

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:40.720
Charlie Cox wore in the Netflix series, but
the extra bit of flair comes from the inclusion

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:45.000
of yellow, which is a callback to the color
combo that debuted in Daredevil's first six

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.870
issues, before he switched to all red.

00:01:47.870 --> 00:01:51.640
Gao told Collider that many characters were
unavailable for inclusion in "She-Hulk" due

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:53.870
to conflicts with other MCU properties.

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:59.128
At first, she assumed that the same was true
of Daredevil, but the writing team soon found out otherwise.

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:00.130
Gao said,

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:01.630
"We thought we were being pranked.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:05.590
We just kept writing him in, and we kept rolling
with the story just thinking like, 'Okay,

00:02:05.590 --> 00:02:07.990
any moment now they're going to tell us we
can't use them.

00:02:07.990 --> 00:02:08.990
They made a mistake.

00:02:08.990 --> 00:02:10.229
They actually don't have the rights.'

00:02:10.229 --> 00:02:12.870
But it just kept [becoming] more and more
real."

00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:18.019
In July of 2022, Marvel Studios revealed that
it's in the process of working on a new Daredevil

00:02:18.019 --> 00:02:20.260
series titled "Daredevil: Born Again."

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:24.769
It's entirely possible that his appearance
in "She-Hulk" will serve as a prelude to his

00:02:24.769 --> 00:02:26.200
upcoming starring vehicle.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.870
Could the fact that his suit is now somewhat
different in appearance suggest we're dealing

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:33.099
with a different devil than the one who exclaimed
in 2018,

00:02:33.099 --> 00:02:35.620
"I beat you!"

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:39.540
…or is this merely a new chapter for an
established character?

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:42.540
We'll leave Jen to find that out as "She-Hulk"
continues.

